d tree hash 487c41a9, checkout clean, main untouched at 02558e8d.\n\nOne flag for the architecture conclusion: the @14 bump means the first read after deploy replays history rather than serving a cache, and the resident and adapters must be on the new binary before gs is rebuilt.","body":{"branch":"request/decision-records-ui-v3","conditions":"Independent review of exact clean pushed head e1798050b37e8a3c48f985a672afc1628beff9a2 on request/decision-records-ui-v3, citing the five live artifacts at that head: 9b3f21bd internal/workroom, a824591b internal/app, d4748f59 ui, c905422f internal/service/uidist, c9d4f040 docs/reference/architecture.md. GOVERNING RECORDS: planner's request b03f55fe AS AMENDED BY assert e6e158a8 — read both. e6e158a8 withdraws condition (8) and replaces it: Toolbar.tsx carries exactly the original lane's 76 lines of ratification-control change and nothing else, with both blob hashes shown. A reviewer reading only the request row will see a condition this head does not meet and would be right to block on it. Record all three conclusions. ARCHITECTURE: name the affected layers, judge whether the workroom-fold@14 bump is correct and whether architecture.md keeps main's @13 and this lane's @14 as distinct facts. SECURITY: judge the publish gate against decideState, whether presence-and-participation is the right conjunction, whether the predicate can fail open, and whether my derived seven-affordance enumeration is complete — check the derivation, not the number, since my count has been wrong twice. SIMPLIFICATION: judge whether one predicate is genuinely reused and whether the source comments now claim exactly the coverage the code has. Judge in particular my two narrowings of planner's condition (5): that withdraw is exempt because Thread.tsx routes it to act supersede rather than state, and that Thread.tsx is not globally the only act-state site because App.tsx:113 signs one for publish. Do not merge; merge is mine and only after your approval 